INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal='Locate single-month volume anomalies in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by computing each region×product_line monthly volume as a multiple of its own 24-month mean, report the top-3 combos with their multiples and return rates, judge whether the spike is real demand or channel stuffing, and save a fully-sourced Markdown report to disk.'):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max of the month column), unique regions, unique product lines, and print first 5 rows as sample → db_agent
2. Compute monthly volume anomaly ratios: Using the CSV, for each (region × product_line) compute the 24-month rolling mean of monthly sales volume, then compute the ratio = current_month_volume / 24-month_mean for every month. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/volume_anomaly_ratios.csv) with columns: region, product_line, month, monthly_volume, mean_24m, ratio → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 anomaly combos & fetch return rates: From the saved ratios CSV, find the top-3 (region, product_line, month) by ratio. For each, look up the corresponding return_rate from the original CSV. Save a small summary CSV (offline_data/top3_anomalies.csv) with columns: rank, region, product_line, month, monthly_volume, mean_24m, ratio, return_rate → code_agent
4. Assess demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 combos, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) return_rate for the anomaly month vs the 24-month average return_rate for that combo, (b) whether the following 1-3 months show a volume drop (reversion), (c) the ratio magnitude. Save a signals CSV (offline_data/stuffing_signals.csv) → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/volume_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing the top-3 combos with all key numbers; (3) every key number annotated with source in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a concluding paragraph judging whether each anomaly is more likely real demand or channel stuffing, with reasoning; (5) embed any charts as base64 or reference saved PNGs. All data must come from the local CSV only. → code_agent
